2. Employee Types

Support the following employee/person types:

Owner

- Full agency access.
- Multiple owners can exist.
- Owners should have substantially similar privileges.
- Owners can manage employees, permissions, targets, policies, commissions, reports and agency configuration.

Co-owner

- Similar privileges to owner.
- Permissions should still be configurable where required.

Sales Employee

Primary responsibilities:

- Lead follow-up
- Customer interaction
- Policy sales
- Renewals
- Cross-selling
- Field visits
- Revenue generation

Back-office Employee

Primary responsibilities:

- Policy processing
- Documentation
- Customer servicing
- Renewal preparation
- Claims assistance
- Data entry
- Administrative tasks

Referral Partner

A referral-oriented role.

Primary responsibilities:

- Refer leads/customers.
- Track referred business.
- View eligible commission information.
- Track referral performance.

Do not make referral partners look like normal employees internally. Their workspace should be a simplified referral/performance workspace.

