12. ACTIVITY LOG / DAILY WORK LOG

Do NOT treat Activity Logs and Tasks as the same thing.

This distinction is important.

Tasks

Work items that are predefined, assigned and tracked.

Activity Logs

A record of what the employee actually did during the day, including work that may not have existed as a predefined task.

Examples:

- Called 12 customers
- Visited 2 customers
- Discussed renewal with client
- Prepared policy documents
- Coordinated with insurer
- Resolved customer query
- Helped colleague with claim documentation

Employees should be able to log:

- Activity
- Category
- Start time
- End time
- Duration
- Related customer/lead/policy if applicable
- Notes
- Outcome

Example:

Activity:
Customer follow-up

Category:
Sales

Duration:
45 minutes

Related:
Amit Sharma

Outcome:
Customer requested quotation.

